# Todonado environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in values from your Supabase project
# (Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API).
# NEVER commit the real .env file — it is gitignored.

# Your Supabase project URL, e.g. https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# Your Supabase "anon" / public key (safe for the browser; RLS protects data)
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — for `npm run seed` ONLY (dev convenience). Never used by the app.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Preferred: the service-role key bypasses RLS to seed the first user's
# workspace. It is a SECRET — keep it only in your local .env (gitignored),
# never expose it to the browser or commit it.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Alternative to the service-role key: seed as a real signed-in user via the
# anon key. Provide the credentials of an existing Todonado account.
# SEED_EMAIL=
# SEED_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Billing (Stripe). Only the VITE_ ones reach the browser; the rest are set in
# Vercel, never here. Full runbook: docs/BILLING_SETUP.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PRICE IDS ARE DECLARED TWICE, AND THE TWO COPIES MUST BE IDENTICAL.
#
# The browser needs them at BUILD time to know what to ask for; the server
# needs them at RUN time to decide what it is willing to sell (audit FLAG-2 —
# the server must never trust a price id from the client, so it cannot simply
# read the client's copy). If they disagree, every checkout returns 400
# invalid_price and the server log says "rejected a price this deployment does
# not sell".
#
# VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_...
# VITE_STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY=price_...   # must equal STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY
# VITE_STRIPE_PRICE_YEARLY=price_...    # must equal STRIPE_PRICE_YEARLY
#
# Server-only (Vercel env vars — never VITE_, never committed):
#
# STRIPE_MODE is the ONE declaration of test vs live. Every key, price and
# retrieved Stripe object is checked against it, and a mismatch fails closed
# rather than being guessed at. It is NOT inferred from whsec_, because a
# webhook signing secret does not encode mode.
# STRIPE_MODE=test                      # or: live
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY=price_...        # must equal VITE_STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY
# STRIPE_PRICE_YEARLY=price_...         # must equal VITE_STRIPE_PRICE_YEARLY
#
# Where Stripe sends people back to after checkout or the customer portal.
# Server-only and deliberately NOT derived from the request's Origin header
# (audit FLAG-4 — a header is attacker-controlled). Optional: unset means
# https://www.todonado.com. Must be an https origin (http allowed only for
# localhost); a value that is not usable is ignored and logged.
# APP_BASE_URL=https://www.todonado.com
